% DUAL FORMULATION NOTE:
% This constraint is part of the 'human dignity and AI governance' constraint family, which decomposes the contested kernel into four structurally distinct readings. Each reading has different ε, different beneficiary/victim structures, different governance implications. The techno-optimist reading claims high coordination value (solving innovation bottleneck) but operates with high extractiveness (concentrating benefits, externalizing costs). Sibling readings in the family offer alternative ε assessments: magisterial integralist would measure low extractiveness (dignity inalienable, not achievement-dependent); secular humanist would measure moderate extractiveness with universal protections; pluralist pragmatic would measure low extractiveness with negotiated inclusion. The readings are linked because each reading's adoption affects the viability and structure of the others — they are not independent constraints but a family of readings of the same kernel. ε-invariance principle: each reading has a single stable ε (the standing arrangement under contest, assessed by that reading's lights), never averaged across readings. The techno-optimist reading assesses ε for the current AI governance arrangement as 0.78 (high extraction, concentrated benefits, excluded voices). A magisterial reading would assess the same empirical arrangement as higher extraction (dignity violated by commodification). A secular humanist would assess it as extraction without proper democratic legitimation. The family is the mechanism for surfacing these divergences.

